    "note-rain": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 560, "top": 512,
      "text": "WHY A COLUMN",
      "fontColor": "#c8d8f0", "fontSize": 13
    },
    "note-rain-body": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 560, "top": 536,
      "text": "Rain falls vertically. Density encodes how hard\nthe session is working — 2 streams idle, 40 under\neffort — and that is the best idea in the DeskLock\ndesign.\n\nA 420px column gives a stream ~38 cells of fall.\nA 90px strip gives it ~4: streams spawn and die\nbefore the density difference is readable, so the\nsignal stops working.\n\nThe column is also chat-shaped, which is what\nEpic E's input box wants: face top, answer middle,\ninput bottom. A strip has nowhere to put an answer.",
      "fontColor": "#c8d0e0", "fontSize": 11
    },
    "note-cost": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 560, "top": 760,
      "text": "COST",
      "fontColor": "#c8d8f0", "fontSize": 13
    },
    "note-cost-body": {
      "type": "Text",
      "left": 560, "top": 784,
      "text": "Permanent horizontal space until collapsed —\nthe real trade. On a 3440px display that is ~5%\nof width; on a 1440px laptop it is ~13% and the\nspine matters more.\n\nBuys D-6 parity for free: isVisible / isCollapsed /\nsizeOf, restart persistence, `clide panel resize`,\nand `clide pane list` reporting, all from being a\nreal slot rather than a widget.",
      "fontColor": "#c8d0e0", "fontSize": 11
    }
  }
